**`SearchTree.java`** (new file) — A generic interface bounded by `T extends Comparable<T>`. The `Comparable` bound is the right constraint here: BST ordering only requires that elements can be compared to each other, not that they implement any BST-specific contract. This lets `BinarySearchTree` be swapped for any other ordered-tree implementation.

